+data-phone rides down the same way and for the same reason. A client-side
+timeout has no response body to carry a number in, so the number has to already
+be on the page. It comes from the hotel row via the site-wide context
+processor, which every page already runs, so this costs no extra query. Empty
+when there is no hotel row, and the JS drops the "call us" half of the message
+rather than offering a blank number to dial.
